{"name":"Marshmallow Whip","hex":"#f9efe0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marshmallow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Marsh mallow, a species of mallow, Althaea officinalis, that grows in marshy terrain. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A type of confectionery, originally (since Ancient Egyptian times) made from this plant, but now generally made of sugar or corn syrup, gelatin that has been presoftened in water, gum arabic, flavorings, and sometimes beaten egg whites, all whipped to a spongy consistency."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To soften (literally or figuratively)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marshmallow"},{"term":"whip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lash; a pliant, flexible instrument, such as a rod (commonly of cane or rattan) or a plaited or braided rope or thong (commonly of leather) used to create a sharp \"crack\" sound for directing or herding animals.","The same instrument used to strike a person or animal for corporal punishment or torture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a whip.","To hit with any flexible object."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marshmallow","blocks":[{"text":"Marshmallow is a confection made from sugar, water and gelatin whipped to a solid-but-soft consistency. It is used as a filling in baking or molded into shapes and coated with corn starch. This sugar confection is inspired by a medicinal confection made from Althaea officinalis, the marsh-mallow plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/White_Marshmallows.jpg/330px-White_Marshmallows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshmallow","wikidata":"Q272198"},{"title":"Whip","blocks":[{"text":"A whip is a blunt weapon or implement used in a striking motion to create sound or pain. Whips can be used for flagellation against humans or animals to exert control or strength through pain compliance or fear of pain, or be used as an audible cue through the distinct whipcrack effect. Whips are commonly used on horses to give subtle cues as tapping. The portion of the whip used for striking is generally either a firm rod designed for direct contact, or a flexible line requiring a specialized swinging motion. The former is easier and more precise, the latter offers longer reach and greater force. Some varieties have an extended stock section in addition to the line."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Riding_crop.jpeg/330px-Riding_crop.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whip","wikidata":"Q152910"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG/500px-Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG/1280px-Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG/500px-Althaea_officinalis_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The marsh-mallow plant (Althaea officinalis)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlthaea_officinalis_002.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg/500px-Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg/1280px-Just_Born_Peeps_in_an_Easter_Basket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikim